---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-kanban</code> is a board of columns whose cards the person moves by drag and drop or
  with the keyboard. It is data-driven: <code>columns</code> is an array of
  <code>{'{'} id, title, limit? {'}'}</code> and <code>cards</code> an array of
  <code>{'{'} id, columnId, title, ... {'}'}</code>, where the order of <code>cards</code> is the
  order within each column. Data, not child elements, because a move is a data change you save, and
  the keyboard can move a card to any column without the board knowing your markup.
</p>
<p>
  <code>renderCard</code> renders a card's content; without it a card shows its
  <code>title</code>. Cards are rendered into the board's light DOM, so your page styles reach
  them. Give the board a height for its columns to scroll; the board scrolls sideways when the
  columns do not fit.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-kanban id='kanban-demo' label='Sprint 12' style='width: 100%; height: 26rem;'></wc-kanban>
  <script is:inline>
    const $board = document.getElementById('kanban-demo');
    $board.columns = [
      { id: 'todo', title: 'To do' },
      { id: 'doing', title: 'In progress' },
      { id: 'review', title: 'Review' },
      { id: 'done', title: 'Done' },
    ];
    $board.cards = [
      { id: '1', columnId: 'todo', title: 'Fix login', owner: 'Ada' },
      { id: '2', columnId: 'todo', title: 'Update icons', owner: 'Grace' },
      { id: '3', columnId: 'todo', title: 'Write release notes', owner: 'Linus' },
      { id: '4', columnId: 'doing', title: 'Table virtual scroll', owner: 'Ada' },
      { id: '5', columnId: 'review', title: 'Dark mode tokens', owner: 'Grace' },
      { id: '6', columnId: 'done', title: 'Pin input', owner: 'Linus' },
    ];
    // Plain JavaScript: return a DOM node (or a string).
    $board.renderCard = card => {
      const content = document.createElement('div');
      content.innerHTML = '<div style="font-weight:500"></div><small style="opacity:.7"></small>';
      content.firstChild.textContent = card.title;
      content.lastChild.textContent = card.owner;
      return content;
    };
    $board.addEventListener('card-move', event => {
      myConsole.log(`card-move ${JSON.stringify(event.detail)}`);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Rendering with Lit</h3>
<pre><code>{`html\`<wc-kanban
  label="Sprint"
  .columns=\${this.columns}
  .cards=\${this.cards}
  .renderCard=\${card => html\`<strong>\${card.title}</strong><p>\${card.owner}</p>\`}
  @card-move=\${(event) => this.save(event.detail)}
></wc-kanban>\`;`}</code></pre>
